{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551391-possible-fallout-of-a-new-mouth-of-peace-exalting-as-a-exigent-or-celestial","id":1551391,"title":"Possible fallout of a new Mouth of Peace Exalting as a Exigent or Celestial?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-01T11:12:43-07:00","id":1551391,"title":"Possible fallout of a new Mouth of Peace Exalting as a Exigent or Celestial?","content":"If the Sidereals select a new mouth of peace exalts not as a dragon-blooded but instead as an Exigent or a Sidereal or Celestial (either managing to pretend she is a dragon-blooded exalt at first or being immediately detected as an Anathema), what kind of political and religious fallout could result?<br /> <br /> For a Sidereal Mouth would it just be business as usual but with the Mouth having more power and not just a puppet? Or would them being a sidereal make it impossible for them also to be a major religious figure since everyone would forget them?<br /> <br /> I know Exigents aren't kill on sight, but it can depend on the god. Would the Mouth be disqualified depending on the god, or if it were say, the god of the Imperial City, would the mouth be allowed to stay the mouth, just with her god getting a talking to?<br /> <br /> If the Mouth exalted as a Solar or Lunar but managed to hide that at first (or was given assistance by the Gold Faction) but was later discovered, would she be killed outright or would this be more likely to result in a religious schism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T12:14:32-07:00","id":1551393,"title":"","content":"It's not spelled out, but it's a reasonable guess that in accordance with the Perfected Hierarchy, the Mouth <i>has</i> to be a Dragon-Blood; Solars and Lunars are Anathema, and most Exigents are the results of improper congress between gods and mortals. At best (Exigent where the blame can firmly be placed on the god), she'd be disqualified; at worst (Solar/Lunar Anathema at the heart of the Order) she'd be killed on discovery, assuming she hadn't made a run for it upon realizing what had happened.<br /> <br /> A Sid Mouth is never happening; Arcane Fate makes it impossible for them to hold positions of long-term open influence, and they long ago adjusted to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T20:33:16-07:00","id":1551403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551391-possible-fallout-of-a-new-mouth-of-peace-exalting-as-a-exigent-or-celestial#post1551391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Sidereals select a new mouth of peace exalts not as a dragon-blooded but instead as an Exigent or a Sidereal or Celestial (either managing to pretend she is a dragon-blooded exalt at first or being immediately detected as an Anathema), what kind of political and religious fallout could result? ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The vetting process for the Mouth of Peace would prevent this. They find a candidate and wait until she's 15. If she Exalts, she's the Mouth. If not, the candidacy is considered a mistake and they move to the next potential candidate.<br /> <br /> In this context, the Mouth probably <i>can't </i>be any of those others since if she Exalts as an Anathema, she's obviously not the reincarnation of the prior Mouth, and if she Exalts as an Exigent, pretty much the same thing since she wasn't the right spritual enlightenment to get the &quot;right&quot; Exaltation anyhow. And if she faked being a Dragon-Blooded to get the position, she'd be pretty much Anathema the moment it is found out since that is a pretty big subversion of the rightful structure of the Immacualte Order there.<br /> <br /> And it's probably not a schism when &quot;We sometimes get the wrong person&quot; and &quot;That person happened to be a fucking Anathema&quot;. It would if anything be a good object lesson in the ways that the Anathema go out to subert the rightful order and all that. <br /> <br /> Note the Gold Faction wouldn't by default help such a person either. Gold doesn't mean pro-Solar/Lunar. It means pro-reform/not status quo. Such a thing would be such a blow-up in general political stability that probably folks proposing it would be a bit far for most folks in the Faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T07:49:24-07:00","id":1551422,"title":"","content":"A Sidereal Mouth of Peace would not happen because Sidereal Exaltation is bestowed at birth and ideally identified well ahead of time. If, in the course of looking for candidates for the next Mouth of Peace, a prospective Sidereal is located, the Sidereals in the search party are going to quietly direct attention away from the future colleague and mark them down as somebody to start bringing into the fold prior to their Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}